jobs.description:
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a&amp;nbsp;Lead Game Designer to join our Monopoly GO! game team remotely within the US!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monopoly GO! is a global phenomenon and the biggest mobile game launch in history, captivating millions of players worldwide. The team is based in Europe and the US, and works every day to create captivating new experiences for our players.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product features end-to-end — from early concept through release, live operations, and post-launch optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the creation of new multiplayer social and/or solo minigames that expand player engagement and enrich the overall gameplay experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate high-level product and franchise objectives into detailed, player-centric feature designs, ensuring clarity and alignment across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain clear, comprehensive game and feature specifications, partnering closely with design to ensure documentation is complete, consistent, and actionable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with design and UX, guiding the direction of designs and ensuring they reflect player needs, franchise goals, and business priorities (without directly managing designers day-to-day).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work deeply cross-functionally with designers, artists, engineers, analysts, and producers to build high-quality features that meet both product and technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing feedback and implementation support, ensuring features progress smoothly through development and match the intended vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of market, genre, and competitive trends to shape an innovative, data-informed roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate strong leadership, influencing team direction, driving alignment, and elevating the quality of execution—beyond just generating ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Potentially mentor or partner closely with designers, with room to grow into management responsibilities over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for F2P Mobile Games: Enthusiastic about working on sophisticated F2P ecosystems, handling diverse player life cycles and spending behaviors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Qualifications: 5+ years in F2P mobile casual games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Skills: Strong verbal and written skills; able to explain the “why” to align the team with the product vision; ability to thrive in global team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Management: Skilled at prioritizing high-impact initiatives, understanding trade-offs, anticipating risks, managing expectations, and ensuring quality deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feature Ownership: Exemplified experience in leading indirect reports toward shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design Expertise: Ability to build experiences that encourage positive player behavior, especially on features without comparables in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantitative Skills: Intermediate statistics; able to assess when and how to use data, translate product issues into analytics tasks, set hypotheses, interpret data optimally, and visualize it in Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical, Analytical, and Creative Thinking: Outcome-driven with a strong focus on execution and an ambitious mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ex

&lt;p&gt;Riot engineers bring deep knowledge of specific technical areas but also value the opportunity to work in a variety of broader domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Unreal Ecosystem (UnEco) team has an impact on a wide array of topics, including runtime performance, tooling, CI/CD, just to name a few. As a Staff Software Engineer on the UnEco team, you&#39;ll drive the technical direction of your team and influence strategy across related teams, building a strong engineering vision and offering creative solutions to technical problems that empower game teams across Riot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team collaborates globally with partners across Riot, all contributing to a stronger, more efficient Unreal development ecosystem. You&#39;ll lead the breakdown of complex, cross-team technical challenges - from build systems to editor tooling to runtime infrastructure - championing solutions in alignment with game teams and partners that empower the developers who depend on your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a full-time role based in Australia (AEST timezone). Internal Job Title: Software Engineer III&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;Sydney-based Rioters work on-site. Remote work is available for candidates elsewhere in AEST-aligned Australia (e.g. Melbourne, Brisbane, Canberra) with Australian work rights. Perth and Darwin are not suitable due to timezone overlap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation &amp;amp; Immigration Support: &lt;/strong&gt;Candidates who require visa sponsorship must be based in, or relocate to, Sydney. Riot offers relocation assistance and will sponsor the appropriate work visa, subject to eligibility and local immigration requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development, and maintenance of shared libraries, plugins, and tools used by multiple game teams - driving platform-wide consistency and maintainability while balancing individual team needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical roadmapping for platform capabilities, setting direction that balances immediate game team needs with long-term architectural vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion technical designs in alignment with game teams and partners, navigating tradeoffs and building consensus across diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and participate in the technical planning process, breaking down multi-month work efforts and sequencing delivery across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold a high standard of engineering excellence. Lead code reviews, drive testing strategy, and contribute to continuous improvement of team and cross-team practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear documentation and communicate technical details across teams and disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and participate in the on-call rotation; resolve live incidents, drive RCAs, and champion systemic fixes to reduce future impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on the team in both technical and soft skills; help level up developers across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, or a comparable field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in professional software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional experience and proficiency with C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software engineering fundamentals (data structures, algorithms, concurrency, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading technical work that impacts multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical direction, designing solutions, and reviewing the designs of others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building software used by other engineering teams and navigating cross-team dependencies, rather than deep single-team, single-feature ownership.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;p&gt;作为一名资深文案策划，您将负责构建和丰富基于全新重社交手游的世界观与叙事体验。您将确保故事情节、角色塑造和包装不仅绝对契合原 IP 的宏大设定，更能完美融入游戏的核心玩法中，为游戏赋予深刻的沉浸感与持久的情感共鸣。您将跨职能协作，确保叙事内容能够高质量、生动地呈现在玩家面前。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;utd37w&quot; data-start=&quot;806&quot; data-end=&quot;824&quot;&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;8oibwx&quot; data-start=&quot;826&quot; data-end=&quot;840&quot;&gt;核心叙事框架与内容设计&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;841&quot; data-end=&quot;934&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1mmicf2&quot; data-start=&quot;841&quot; data-end=&quot;894&quot;&gt;深度参与产品叙事框架、内容结构及核心角色表达的规划与设计，推动叙事 DEMO 方案高效实现与快速落地。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;vtjg3v&quot; data-start=&quot;895&quot; data-end=&quot;934&quot;&gt;负责长期内容体验的叙事包装与表达设计，确保内容风格统一且具备持续演进能力。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;z2q8ye&quot; data-start=&quot;936&quot; data-end=&quot;951&quot;&gt;高品质文案撰写与内容表达&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;952&quot; data-end=&quot;1033&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1aipl1g&quot; data-start=&quot;952&quot; data-end=&quot;1001&quot;&gt;负责产品内核心文案的撰写与包装，包括系统文本、角色语音文本（VO）、交互事件及长期运营内容等。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1uj4pvn&quot; data-start=&quot;1002&quot; data-end=&quot;1033&quot;&gt;确保整体内容表达在语气、结构与沉浸感层面保持高质量一致性。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1njhp1a&quot; data-start=&quot;1035&quot; data-end=&quot;1047&quot;&gt;内容研究与创新探索&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1048&quot; data-end=&quot;1124&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;cdpggt&quot; data-start=&quot;1048&quot; data-end=&quot;1087&quot;&gt;深度研究行业内主流产品的叙事表达方式与内容趋势，探索创新性的互动内容体验。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1v3prx2&quot; data-start=&quot;1088&quot; data-end=&quot;1124&quot;&gt;结合用户反馈与市场变化，为长期内容迭代提供高质量创意方向与表达方案。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;2vvy1f&quot; data-start=&quot;1126&quot; data-end=&quot;1139&quot;&gt;跨团队协作与落地推进&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1140&quot; data-end=&quot;1214&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;ecdms7&quot; data-start=&quot;1140&quot; data-end=&quot;1177&quot;&gt;编写高标准叙事文档与内容需求文档，清晰定义视听表达需求与内容实现标准。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1mjckvh&quot; data-start=&quot;1178&quot; data-end=&quot;1214&quot;&gt;主动协调美术、音频、设计、工程与制作团队，高效推进关键内容方案落地。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;a0vzwk&quot; data-start=&quot;1216&quot; data-end=&quot;1225&quot;&gt;用户体验洞察&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1226&quot; data-end=&quot;1289&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;fy4asa&quot; data-start=&quot;1226&quot; data-end=&quot;1261&quot;&gt;深入理解目标用户体验需求，通过内容表达增强产品沉浸感与长期参与感。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1fkvn28&quot; data-start=&quot;1262&quot; data-end=&quot;1289&quot;&gt;系统性评估内容方案的创新性、可行性与整体体验价值。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;6uehu5&quot; data-start=&quot;1296&quot; data-end=&quot;1321&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1323&quot; data-end=&quot;1590&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;ushozx&quot; data-start=&quot;1323&quot; data-end=&quot;1356&quot;&gt;本科及以上学历，6年以上互动娱乐或游戏内容设计/文案策划经验。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1w6u629&quot; data-start=&quot;1357&quot; data-end=&quot;1402&quot;&gt;具备大型在线产品或长线运营内容项目经验，曾参与新项目从研发到上线或核心开发阶段者优先。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;18a03r8&quot; data-start=&quot;1403&quot; data-end=&quot;1442&quot;&gt;拥有扎实的文学功底与叙事设计能力，能够独立完成长线内容规划与角色表达设计。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;2dmlzk&quot; data-start=&quot;1443&quot; data-end=&quot;1480&quot;&gt;具备优秀的跨团队沟通与协作能力，能够将抽象概念转化为可执行的内容需求。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;2phrxv&quot; data-start=&quot;1481&quot; data-end=&quot;1518&quot;&gt;具备优秀的文字审美与内容把控能力，能够在复杂项目环境下保持高质量输出。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;5fd4lp&quot; data-start=&quot;1519&quot; data-end=&quot;1541&quot;&gt;对互动体验与沉浸式内容表达具备深入理解。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;x26ord&quot; data-start=&quot;1542&quot; data-end=&quot;1570&quot;&gt;具备良好的逻辑分析能力、信息整合能力与文档表达能力。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;cxgwgw&quot; data-start=&q

&lt;p&gt;Technical Game Designers on the Teamfight Tactics team are game designers who also have access to the C++ code base. They apply the team’s engineering principles to technical design work, improve and add to existing design tools to unblock design tasks (sometimes unblocking themselves, in their game design role!), and own gameplay and systems design areas. Their game design expertise lets them dream up and create memorable gameplay experiences for TFT players, and their technical expertise lets them deliver those experiences in a robust, sustainable, and elegant way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Technical Design Manager on the Teamfight Tactics team&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll manage Technical Game Designers across the project. You&#39;ll see to their career progress, evaluate their technical and game design contributions, bring out their best work, and ensure they&#39;re delivering on their teams&#39; goals. In turn, you&#39;ll report to the Design Director, helping to build the Technical Game Design subdiscipline on the team and for League Studios, and maximizing the TD group’s impact. But: on the Teamfight Tactics team, design managers often take on individual contributions, so you’ll have plenty of chances to exercise your own craft as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the project’s technical game designers: help them grow, learn, and perform to their potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high craft bar: Ensure that the work you oversee meets Riot&#39;s demanding craft standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for players: Stay in tune with the player experience and know how to understand and incorporate their feedback into roadmaps and feature decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and build trust: Work closely with other discipline leads and managers to ensure Tech Design is delivering what they need, when they need it; ensure that features can be scoped efficiently so project plans can be built; and foster relationships with teams outside of Teamfight Tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong teams: Take an active role in recruiting and onboarding to ensure capable technical game designers join our teams and ramp up quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience as a technical game designer, gameplay engineer, or some similar position closely associated with both technical and game design work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience as a manager, team lead, or discipline leader (can overlap with the above requirement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft: Craft interviews for this role will look at both gameplay engineering and game design skills; we’d like to see Senior level craft expertise in one, but not necessarily both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Management: You&#39;ll need leadership experience resolving conflict within and across teams and fostering healthy team culture, along with examples of managing other designers with positive results: promotion, performance improvement, and strong delivery to players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High familiarity with Teamfight Tactics, or willingness to rapidly build that familiarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience as a manager or team lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience as a technical game designer or gameplay engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing both junior and senior designers or engineers - striking the right balance of assistance and autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a live service game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep engagement with Teamfight Tactics over multiple sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the Unreal Engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise and a collaborative spirit that prioritizes the delight of players. We will look at your past studie

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title, League of Legends, to critical and player acclaim. Players form the foundation of our community, and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the League of Legends experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That’s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Rendering Technical Artist (Contract) &lt;/strong&gt;on the Singapore League of Legends PC Team, you’ll help bring the world of Runeterra and beyond to life through materials, lighting, and real-time rendering. League’s visual targets are built on a modern real-time, PBR-based rendering pipeline with stylized, hand-painted treatments, and you’ll author, extend, and maintain the shaders and materials that realize them across champions, skins, and related content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with artists, designers, engineers, and external partners, you’ll act as a bridge between art and engineering—translating visual and art-direction goals into robust, performant solutions that behave consistently across around-game and in-game environments. As an experienced technical artist, you’ll also diagnose rendering issues early, reduce rework, and help raise the craft bar for how shaders and materials are authored across internal and external teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Technical Art Manager, you will ensure that assets meet technical performance standards and artistic direction requirements. In collaboration with Art, Design, Engineering, and external partners, you will contribute to production support and workflow improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that Riot Games does not offer relocation packages for this position. You need to be able to work legally in Singapore, without Riot Games’ sponsorship, to be considered.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author, extend, and maintain real-time shaders and materials for League of Legends within a PBR-based rendering workflow, including reusable shader functions and shared material systems that scale across champions and skins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong PBR fundamentals across albedo, normal, roughness, metallic, ambient occlusion, emissive, lighting, and reflection-probe inputs, ensuring shader features account for the full material response rather than the diffuse channel in isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with Art and Design to understand desired visual behaviors and art direction, and translate them into clear, achievable, and performant rendering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical support to internal and external vendor artists, helping them author, integrate, and troubleshoot materials and shaders for Epic and Legendary skins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate assets across neutral lighting, around-game, and in-game environments and applicable quality levels, diagnosing issues involving lighting, shadows, material response, shader parameters, and texture inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering to manage in-game memory budgets, profile shader and rendering cost, and optimize game performance using tools such as RenderDoc or equivalent GPU-capture tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate visual assets from external vendors into the game engine using Perforce, working closely with the Art Director and Te

&lt;p&gt;Riot Games was established in 2006 by entrepreneurial gamers who believe that player-focused game development can result in great games. In 2009, Riot released its debut title&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;to critical and player acclaim. As the most played video game in the world, over 100 million play every month. Players form the foundation of our community and it’s for them that we continue to evolve and improve the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for humble but ambitious, razor-sharp professionals who can teach us a thing or two. We promise to return the favor. Like us, you take play seriously; you’re passionate about games. We embrace those who see things differently, aren’t afraid to experiment, and who have a healthy disregard for constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&#39;s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Game Designer on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;League of Legends: Wild Rift&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own and evolve the map layouts, terrain architecture, neutral objectives, and jungle monster systems that drive the strategic depth and pacing of Summoner’s Rift. You will design, implement, and optimize core map features, ensuring they deliver an engaging, fair, and dynamically competitive environment optimized for a mobile audience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with Balance and System designers to integrate structural map changes and objective reworks into the core SR gameplay. You will utilize your spatial design expertise and player empathy to navigate complex design challenges, ensuring every environmental and objective adjustment aligns with Riot&#39;s design philosophy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the lifecycle, structural map design, and live iteration of core map features, neutral objectives, and jungle monster mechanics on Summoner&#39;s Rift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set quality and execution standards for terrain layout, map visibility, and objective mechanics, delivering high-clarity documentation that enables seamless cross-functional implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Balance Designer and System Designer to ensure all map terrain changes, objective overhauls, or monster system adaptations safeguard competitive integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize player feedback, high-level telemetry, and game data to diagnose systemic flaws or communication bottlenecks, driving long-term map and environmental updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in professional Game Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in either Map Design or Level Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can create complex mechanics and systems with attention to the player impacts and downstream effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep level of understanding, passion, and engagement with MOBA games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on a live product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is familiar with the LoL IP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise, a collaborative spirit, and decision-making that prioritizes the delight of players. We will be looking at your past studies, experience, and your personal relationship with games.

&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity aid in crafting in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to innovate and iterate player-focused designs that&#39;ll delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Sr. Manager, Game Design &lt;/strong&gt;on an unpublished R&amp;amp;D product, you will help decipher one of Riot’s next big bets. You will help prove an innovative game concept in the early stages of development. You’ll partner with other designers, artists, and engineers to innovate and iterate player-focused designs that aim at delivering a groundbreaking experience. As a you’ll participate in the hiring process of the multiple design teams, manage the team to ensure consistent quality across all, and mentor designers in their professional development. You will report to the Director of Game Design on the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage multiple teams of designers spanning multiple design sub-disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, manage, and mentor design teams tackling multiple design challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with the design team and team leads to create a great holistic experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear design documentation that can be evaluated and implemented by non-designers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help guide the project from pre-production to launch and ongoing live support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience managing design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience working in game design or a similar field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has owned major feature work including directing multi-discipline teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the early-prototype phase of development on at least one game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with game engines (i.e. Unreal, Unity, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise and a collaborative spirit that prioritizes the delight of players. We will look at your past studies and experience, but for this role, we also look for dedicated people with a personal relationship with games. If you embody player empathy and care about players&#39; experiences, this is the role for you!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Riot focuses on work/life balance, shown by our open paid time off policy and other perks such as flexible work schedules. We offer medical, dental, and life insurance, parental leave for you, your spouse/domestic partner, and children, and a 401k with company match. Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/work-with-us/overview&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;benefits pages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Riot Games, we&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;put players first&lt;/a&gt;. That mission drives every decision in our quest to create games and experiences that make it better to be a player. Whether you’re working directly on a new player-facing experience or you’re supporting the company as a whole, everyone at Riot is part of our mission. And just like in our games, we’re better when we work together. Our goal is to create collaborative teams where you are empowered to bring your unique perspective everyday. If that sounds like the kind of place you want to work, we’re looking forward to your app

